This software contains data tables generated from the following third-party sources
(the scripts in tools/ regenerate them). Their licences and credits apply to that data:

- NREL 5-MW reference wind turbine blade and airfoil polars (src/wind/nrel5mw.ts)
  from OpenFAST r-test, https://github.com/OpenFAST/r-test — Apache License 2.0.
  Jonkman, J., Butterfield, S., Musial, W., Scott, G. (2009). Definition of a 5-MW
  Reference Wind Turbine for Offshore System Development. NREL/TP-500-38060.

- Water/steam and refrigerant properties (src/thermo/tables.ts) computed with CoolProp,
  https://github.com/CoolProp/CoolProp — MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2012-2018 Ian H. Bell and other CoolProp developers.
  Bell, I. H., Wronski, J., Quoilin, S., Lemort, V. (2014). Pure and Pseudo-pure Fluid
  Thermophysical Property Evaluation and the Open-Source Thermophysical Property Library
  CoolProp. Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 53(6), 2498–2508.

- Monthly solar climatology for the 81 provinces of Türkiye (src/solar/climateTR.ts)
  from the NASA POWER project, https://power.larc.nasa.gov — "These data were obtained
  from the NASA Langley Research Center (LaRC) POWER Project funded through the NASA
  Earth Science/Applied Science Program."

- Rocket combustion properties (src/aero/ceaTables.ts) computed with NASA CEA
  (Chemical Equilibrium with Applications, NASA Glenn Research Center, Gordon and McBride)
  through RocketCEA, https://rocketcea.readthedocs.io.

- Photon attenuation data (src/nuclear/shieldTables.ts) from XrayDB
  (Elam, Ravel, Sieber tables), https://github.com/xraypy/XrayDB — CC0-1.0 (public domain);
  buildup factors from the project's own Monte Carlo calculation.

Standards, textbooks and papers cited in the source comments and test names are references
for the methods. Some modules contain numerical values taken from tables of standards and
catalogues because the calculation needs them (for example ISO 286 tolerance grades and
fundamental deviations, ISO 18265 hardness conversion rows, EN 10365 section dimensions,
typical rolling-bearing catalogue values). No text of those works is reproduced; consult the
standards themselves for authoritative values.
